Package: phcc
Version: 0.0.2
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: PYMEHackers <admin@pymehackers.com>
Depends: libc6, libgtk-3-0, libayatana-appindicator3-1, libglib2.0-0, procps, util-linux, bash, curl, jq, ca-certificates, pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: libnotify-bin
Homepage: https://github.com/pymehackers/PHCC
Description: PYMEHackers Control Center - core (top bar indicator)
 PYMEHackers Control Center is the core of the PYMEHackers platform. It places an icon in the top
 bar of the desktop that opens the PYMEHackers Control Center menu with the "Systems" and
 "Cybersecurity" sections. Each section lists the installed modules and their actions.
 .
 Module discovery is dynamic: each module (for example phcc-mod-port-sentinel) installs a
 manifest in /usr/share/pymehackers/modules/<section>/ and appears in the menu automatically,
 without reconfiguring the core.
 .
 The "Module catalog" menu lists the modules published in the PHCC-modules repository
 (https://github.com/pymehackers/PHCC-modules) and installs, updates, reinstalls or uninstalls
 them directly from there, after an administrator authentication (pkexec).
 .
 It ships two ways of showing the icon: an AppIndicator (phcc binary, for MATE, XFCE, Cinnamon,
 KDE, Unity...) and a native GNOME Shell extension (phcc@pymehackers.com), so GNOME does not need
 gnome-shell-extension-appindicator. It adds a "PYMEHackers Control Center" launcher to the
 applications menu that shows the icon on any desktop; on GNOME the extension also enables itself
 at login, and on the other desktops the AppIndicator starts with the session. The module
 services keep working independently of the indicator.
